comparison the query is expanded through \code{synonyms}: a query word in a
synonym group brings in the rest of that group at \code{synonym_weight},
which is what carries \code{"stomach upset"} across to \code{"nauseous"}.
\item \strong{Fuzzy similarity} (weight \code{weights["ngram"]}). The same cosine,
computed over character 3-grams instead of words. This is what tolerates
typos, plurals and word endings the stemmer misses.
